  "title": "The model menu got considerably wider",
  "summary": "The model menu grew across text, images, and video, while apps and account tools got better at helping people use it.\n\nQwen brought code, long-context reasoning, and vision models. Nova and Grok gained new chat options, while `midijourney` gained two tiers. The `nova` alias now points to Nova 2 Lite; the main site separately switched its default text model to `nova-fast`. Models backed by four broken providers were removed from the registry. More choices are useful; choices that cannot answer are less so.\n\nNova Canvas, Qwen Image, and Grok Imagine added image generation or editing options. Nova Reel, Grok video, `wan-fast`, and the returning LTX-2 expanded video generation. Follow-up work corrected image input for `grok-video-pro` and routing for LTX-2. Video models that support audio now default to including it, with `audio=false` available when silence is the point.\n\nRegistered SPORE users can now submit apps to the Greenhouse. Review changes preserve submitted names and fuller descriptions, while catalog cleanup removed duplicate old-format rows without discarding apps found only there. New projects covered teaching, language practice, creative tools, terminal workflows, and more; the README also began crediting recent app creators by name.\n\nA device-code login flow gives CLIs and headless apps a browser-based way to connect. The dashboard explains API Keys and App Keys more clearly, and Spore-to-Seed checks now survive GitHub username changes. Websim gained a working prompt-and-model starting point; the Elevator Challenge added account connection and model choice; CatGPT now uses a signed-in player's key and handles shared model selections more reliably.",
  "pr_count": 99,
